Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] docs: kanban stranded-park escalation and its config
 keys

Co-Authored-By: Contributor <contributor@example.com>
---
 website/docs/user-guide/features/kanban.md | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/website/docs/user-guide/features/kanban.md b/website/docs/user-guide/features/kanban.md
index b5938840be..9d5469cbac 100644
--- a/website/docs/user-guide/features/kanban.md
+++ b/website/docs/user-guide/features/kanban.md
@@ -702,6 +702,23 @@ Each stop records its producer in `spend_budget_decision_ready.producer`: owning
 receive one Kanban notice with spend and decision options, or a card with no
 chat gets one board-supervisor decision card. The supervisor uses
 `kanban.orchestrator_profile`, falling back to `default`. No Inbox post is made.
+A local owning chat that is archived, hidden or gone, or ended and idle longer
+than `kanban.stranded_owner_idle_seconds` (default 86400), is not a route: the
+decision then goes to the supervisor card.
+
+**Stranded parked cards.** A parked card (`triage` or `blocked`) never stays
+invisible. Every `kanban.stranded_sweep_interval_seconds` (default 300) the
+dispatcher checks this board's own parked cards. A card parked longer than
+`kanban.stranded_park_seconds` (default 7200) with no valid human request and no
+live owner is escalated once per park episode. An owner is a live chat, an open
+spend-decision or recovery card, or the stale-triage sweep for up to
+`kanban.stranded_stale_defer_seconds` (default 21600). Dependency and time waits,
+wake checks, lane gates and shared-blocker parks are left alone. The escalation
+stores a human request (Unblock = release it, with `hermes kanban promote` for a
+spend stop; archive = drop it), so the card paints its chats red, and binds the
+desk chat named by `kanban.triage_owner_chat` (`<gateway>/<profile>/<session>`,
+empty = none). A contained card gets only the desk link: containment refuses the
+request write.
 
 When the stopped card lives on another gateway, that decision card's worker
 releases it with one operator call, never an unblock:
